{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24022 - PROTEIN:5821",
  "verbalization": "Miyabenol A appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to MOVP-3 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Miyabenol A acts as a target for Ataxin-2 and 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, both of which are targets of a compound with a complex chemical structure. This compound, 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol, is implicated in the regulation of MOVP-3. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Miyabenol A to MOVP-3 indicates a potential mechanism involving the modulation of proteasome activity or the regulation of Ataxin-2, which in turn influences MOVP-3. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of the compound in orchestrating a network of molecular interactions that ultimately affect MOVP-3.",
